WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:05.420
Crow and Gongenzaka were the first 
to fight in the Friendship Cup.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.930
Crow was so worried about the kids, 
he couldn't focus on the duel.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:13.230
Gongenzaka accepted those feelings.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.850
The duel, between two who 
understood one another,

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:21.430
touched the hearts of the spectators, 
who'd been arguing about Jack.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.770
And in the end, it earned a 
huge round of applause.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.580
D-Wheels.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.760
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.480
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.920
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.120
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:20.750
City's Light and Shadow

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.820
Crow Hogan, who won the first 
match of the tournament,

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:31.930
is leaving the Duel Palace in a sea of applause.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.330
I wasn't sure at first, but that was a great match!

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:39.770
It was so fun!

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.010
Keep it up for the next round, Crow!

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.210
This Gongenzaka duelist...

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:50.650
I never knew you could duel so well 
without using spell or trap cards.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:55.820
If he were a duelist born in City, 
I'd gladly back him financially.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:59.220
It's a shame we won't be 
seeing any more of him.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.320
What a fabulous sight...

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:05.580
This is how the Friendship Cup should be!

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.620
City really is united as one! We're all friends!

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:15.910
Gongenzaka...

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:26.380
Gongenzaka won't be able to stay here anymore.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:33.500
The sixteen of you will spend the 
tournament in these penthouses.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:37.480
However, you can only remain for 
as long as you keep winning.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.690
If you lose, you'll be kicked out immediately.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:44.420
After being driven from his room, 
where will Gongenzaka go?

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:47.940
He won't be taken back to the prison, will he?

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:54.270
I was allowed to stay, even though 
I lost the exhibition match.

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.440
But Gongenzaka lost in the tournament proper.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.740
The door's unlocking?

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.420
Will I already be next to fight?

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:05.390
But I haven't found it yet...

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.260
How will I get closer to Jack?

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.860
Can I fight a duel that isn't just self-satisfaction?

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.840
I haven't found that answer yet!

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.200
Hey! How are you doing, Yuya?

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.740
Mr. Tokumatsu?!

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:23.940
You're too loud! What if someone overhears?

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.380
How did you get in?

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:28.550
I thought we couldn't leave our rooms.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:33.320
Well, it takes a shrimp to know a snake.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:34.140
A shrimp?

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:36.220
Did I get it wrong?

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:37.870
"To catch a carp, you need a shrimp"?

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:39.720
"Meditate for three years atop a shrimp"?

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.290
"The road to hell is paved with shrimp"?

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:45.210
Look... Forget the sayings, okay?

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.000
Hurry it up!

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.470
If you're discovered, I'll be punished, too.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.590
You're bribing them with rare cards again?

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.850
I told you, keep it down!

00:04:57.850 --> 00:05:01.700
But isn't the Administrative Council 
monitoring our rooms?

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.500
What?!

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:08.910
Well, no helping it now.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.620
This was the only way I could see you.

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:15.800
That isn't good! Let's go back right now!

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:17.600
This is really bad!

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:21.160
Shut up! In for a penny, in for a pound.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:24.320
We're all in this together. Give it up!

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.100
Oh, no...

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.310
So, what did you need so bad?

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:33.280
The truth is that I heard a rumor...

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:35.750
A rumor?

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:39.440
Yeah. Not him...

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:43.460
But I heard some other guys 
talking in front of my room.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:46.730
They're acting pretty high and mighty,

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:51.350
using these luxurious rooms, even if 
they're only for the tournament.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:55.530
Despite Crow, Shinji, and Tokumatsu 
being Commons like us.

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:59.260
Just because they're in the Friendship 
Cup, they're treated like Tops!

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:02.340
I don't like it... I hope those fools lose.

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:08.460
And just when I thought I'd have a word 
with those petty, little men...

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:15.310
Do you guys know what happens 
to the duelists that lose?

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:19.760
Well, they're kicked out immediately, right?

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:22.000
They're not just thrown out.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.750
Rumors say they're taken to a certain place.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.220
Like the prison?

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:28.330
Even worse.

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:29.660
Even worse?

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:30.900
Where is it?

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:33.870
These are just rumors, of course.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:40.140
Deep below City, there's a large 
garbage-processing facility.

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:43.140
And they're made to do forced labor there.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:47.550
Forced labor? At an underground 
garbage-processing facility?

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:50.810
Yeah, that's what he said.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.630
It's all just a rumor, obviously.

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:57.300
But I think it's likely to be true.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:01.340
I heard similar rumors in prison.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:02.430
Similar rumors?

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:06.010
That guys who attempted jail breaks 
were sent somewhere.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.040
When something like this happens,

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:12.480
all the people left behind share 
responsibility and punishment.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:16.450
Wherever they're taken, no one's ever come back.

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:22.620
So you think the punishment is forced labor 
in the garbage-processing facility?

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:24.040
Yeah.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:28.330
They'd be forced to work until 
they collapsed... And then...

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.900
That's why no one ever came back.

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:36.440
If you wonder why there's something 
like that under City,

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:39.030
just think about it a little while.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:42.610
It's how this town works.

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:45.840
It's always been a metropolis.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:50.600
But in the ten years I've been in prison, 
City has gotten even bigger.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:56.680
Over ten million people are cramped 
together on this tiny plot of land.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:00.620
The Commons who make up 99% of that figure

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.330
live in poverty, as they always have.

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:06.800
But the mere 1% of the population...

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:09.630
About 100,000 Tops

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:14.540
live in the lap of luxury, like never before.

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:21.220
And they produce a tremendous 
amount of garbage.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:30.460
The people in power built a facility deep 
underground to deal with their trash.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:34.920
But of course, the Tops who 
generate that garbage

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:37.340
refuse to dirty their hands with it.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:42.170
They push that work on the Commons, 
as if it went without saying.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:45.850
They give them forced labor 
to atone for their crimes.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:47.410
That's awful.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:53.290
They put us in these luxurious rooms... 
And if we lose, it's right to the basement.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:56.250
Truly a move from heaven to hell.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:00.390
Then, Gongenzaka is being sent 
to that forced-labor facility?

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:03.350
Most likely.

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:04.760
No!

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:08.590
Well, now you're all excited, so let's 
move on to the second fight.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:13.060
Which duelists will be chosen?

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:16.030
Shinji Weber!

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:20.000
And the year's youngest participant,

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:22.970
Layra Akaba!

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:24.440
Layra?

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:35.350
Master Layra, I'll escort you to the Duel Palace.

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:40.300
Master Layra?

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:44.300
Layra.

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:47.800
Brother...

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:49.370
What are you doing?

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:56.940
Come along now, Layra.

00:09:57.960 --> 00:09:59.430
No need to be afraid.

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.320
What's wrong, Layra?

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:06.880
Why are you defying me?

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:08.290
I-I'm not!

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:09.980
Then, go.

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:14.500
Show the people of this dimension 
what you can do.

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:22.960
No...

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:25.140
No.

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:29.510
No! I don't want to go!

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:31.480
Wait!

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:33.380
Don't, Tsukikage.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.120
I'll go.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:36.810
Yes, sir.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:44.270
He'll make Layra fight a riding duel, too?

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:46.700
What, you didn't know?

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:50.290
I wasn't sure if that would be okay, either...

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:53.130
Of course it isn't okay!

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.330
Layra's still in the Junior Class.

00:10:56.330 --> 00:11:00.140
He hasn't even fought a Real 
Solid Vision duel yet.

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:03.110
I don't understand anything you just said.

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:07.880
But I'm against dragging a little 
kid into a tournament, too...

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:09.760
Of course you are.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:13.610
And if he loses, Layra will be 
sent to do forced labor.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.920
Um, can I go yet?

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:19.090
I'm really gonna be in trouble—

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:23.290
Layra! What are you doing here?

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:28.730
L-Layra... What's wrong?

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:33.080
Excuse me.

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:35.210
You're...

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:40.310
Reiji Akaba!

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:52.860
Layra...

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:00.030
What are you thinking?

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:03.430
Why do you have to make Layra fight?

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:06.330
Layra's still a kid.

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:09.850
Even at LDS, he's still Junior Class, right?

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:15.690
Why does he have to be unwillingly 
dragged into a tournament

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:17.560
against the King of Duelists, Jack Atlas?

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:20.520
No, even before that...

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:23.690
Why did you put Layra in the Lancers?

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:29.390
I came across dimensions, of my 
own free will, to save Yuzu.

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:33.050
Gongenzaka, Kurosaki, Serena...

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:37.140
They all joined the Lancers for 
their own reasons, too.

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:42.330
We're prepared for the danger we'll 
face in the fight with Academia.

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:45.240
I'm sure that's the case for everyone.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:47.810
But Layra...

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:50.280
This little boy, Layra...

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:53.250
I can't imagine he came here of his own will!

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:56.950
You brought him here! Isn't that right?

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:00.160
Why would you bring Layra...

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:04.460
Why would you bring this small child with you?!

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:05.660
Answer me...

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:08.420
Reiji Akaba!

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:15.870
Yuya...

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:17.240
Very well.

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:19.590
I will answer your question.

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:24.980
First, why did I force Layra to take 
part in the Friendship Cup?

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:29.020
To give Layra more experience in 
an actual combat situation.

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:30.620
An actual combat situation?

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:32.620
Don't be ridiculous! Layra's only Junior—

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:35.360
I know what Layra can do...

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:39.920
His ability is on a par with yours.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:42.430
Even if he has talent, Layra is still—

00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:47.040
Then, why did I have Layra join the Lancers?

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:51.640
True, he did not choose to 
join of his own accord.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:55.100
He was following my orders.

00:13:55.820 --> 00:14:00.030
Now, why did I force Layra to join?

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:01.960
That is because...

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:08.460
Layra may be needed in the 
fight against Academia.

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:13.200
Needed? Layra, needed in the 
fight against Academia?

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.890
What are you talking about?

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:20.140
How could a child be necessary for a fight?

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:23.020
Whether or not you believe me—

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:23.840
Shut up.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:25.610
Someday, you'll see the truth.

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:27.540
I told you to shut up!

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.080
Hey, Yuya...

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:34.890
Yuya...

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:47.470
Look! I'm seriously gonna be in trouble!

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:50.090
If they find out I broke the rules 
and opened the door...

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:53.690
If I'm fired, I don't know what 
will happen to me!

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:57.380
I'm returning that, so don't 
tell them I was involved!

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:05.280
Layra... Ever since we came to 
this city, he's been frightened.

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:09.220
Wh-Where is my brother?

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:14.680
Even after Crow saved us, he was 
always curled up alone...

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:18.630
Or so I thought, but he said he 
was searching for you.

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:21.580
Layra, what's wrong?

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:23.790
I'm going to find my brother!

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:24.370
No!

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:30.330
S-Sorry. I'm not angry with you.

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:32.490
Brother...

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:37.300
Right now, it's dangerous for 
us to walk around in City.

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:39.530
Crow told us that.

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:43.030
For now, let's wait. Okay, Layra?

00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:47.590
Even after that, he still wants you.

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:49.730
He respects you.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:54.200
But you only brought him because 
you need him for a fight?

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:55.920
Give me a break!

00:15:55.920 --> 00:15:58.220
I won't make Layra do that!

00:15:58.220 --> 00:15:59.670
I won't let him fight!

00:16:00.260 --> 00:16:05.600
I won't let Layra take part in a fight 
where losing might get him sent

00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:07.380
to a hard-labor facility!

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:10.340
If you won't protect Layra...

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:14.020
Then I will!

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:27.870
Layra...

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:31.140
Answer my question.

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:36.340
Why don't you want to fight?

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:38.810
Because he's afraid, obviously!

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:42.450
I'm asking Layra. Answer me.

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:44.150
Stop forcing him!

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:47.620
Answer me, Layra.

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:56.650
C-Crow's... friend...

00:16:58.690 --> 00:17:01.800
He gave me... candy.

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:04.730
Back then...

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:09.470
You, too! There's plenty, so help yourself.

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:13.040
Helpful provisions from our fellow Commons.

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:14.250
Eat them and be grateful.

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:19.800
Layra remembered, and that's why...

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:20.870
I see.

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:25.860
You don't want to fight someone 
who showed you kindness.

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:27.530
Tsukikage...

00:17:27.530 --> 00:17:28.180
Sir.

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:30.620
You will fight in Layra's place.

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:31.660
Yes, sir.

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:55.450
Brother! Brother!

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:57.280
Brother!

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:57.920
Layra!

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:03.470
Don't be mad, Brother!

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:06.360
I'll do whatever you say...

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:09.150
I'll always do what you say!

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:11.840
I'll always do it... So, please...

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:14.120
I'm not angry.

00:18:14.790 --> 00:18:16.750
Actually, I am very happy.

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:23.720
You have shown that you're 
acquiring a will of your own.

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:26.620
A will of his own?

00:18:27.490 --> 00:18:32.340
The ego's development greatly 
feeds a duelist's growth.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:37.930
It becomes the foothold for devising one's 
own strategies and practicing them.

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:43.030
Wait!

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:47.000
Do you still intend to make Layra fight?

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:52.300
Wait! Hey, come back, Layra!

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:52.940
Hold it!

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:56.730
You're the one who said not to be reckless.

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:02.150
It might be hard for you... But it's 
clear that kid, Layra,

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:06.910
likes the boy with glasses more than you.

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:10.890
You can't pull him 
away against his wishes.

00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:13.440
Um, excuse me.

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:16.310
Could you return to your rooms?

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:36.330
Layra...

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:43.060
A will of his own...

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:53.320
No will of his own?

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:54.210
No.

00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:57.450
That boy has no will of his own.

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:00.120
He has no desires,

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:05.550
no wish for what he wants to become.

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:09.470
The researchers believe it is 
a self-defense mechanism,

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:15.040
developed for survival in that harsh environment.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:16.530
Harsh environment?

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:19.580
Where was he taken from?

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:23.000
A war-torn region in a certain country.

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:28.090
There, fighting has raged for decades.

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:34.250
With no family, and no one to ask for help, 
to continue living in a place like that,

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:40.920
he abandoned himself and acquired the power 
to be whatever someone wanted him to be.

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:43.620
Be whatever someone wanted?

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:46.390
He can become absolutely anything.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:50.520
He completely absorbs the orders of others,

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:54.870
becomes their vessel, and lives for their will alone.

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:58.840
He is a puppet in every respect...

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:02.810
That is why he could become 
a useful asset for us.

00:21:03.350 --> 00:21:06.490
Do you not agree, Reiji?

00:21:09.970 --> 00:21:13.990
If Mother knew, I'm sure she'd disapprove.

00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:24.500
She'd say that a puppet mustn't have a heart.

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:29.710
I'm so sorry for the long wait.

00:21:29.710 --> 00:21:32.120
We had a bit of trouble

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:36.060
that delayed the participants' 
entry into the arena, but...

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:40.250
Once more, let me introduce. 
Today's second match will be

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:44.760
Shinji Weber versus

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:49.040
Layra Akaba!

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:51.850
Wait... A ninja?

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:53.940
Is Layra a ninja?

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:57.080
The tournament's youngest competitor is a ninja?

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:58.120
Huh?

00:21:58.120 --> 00:21:59.380
He isn't?

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:01.130
What's going on here?

00:22:01.510 --> 00:22:04.040
Just who is that ninja?

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:06.100
Not even I know what's going on here!

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:10.540
Tsukikage is fighting in Layra's place?

00:23:48.970 --> 00:23:53.530
You Tops caught me while I 
was escaping from prison,

00:23:53.530 --> 00:23:57.070
and put me here to make an example out of me.

00:23:57.070 --> 00:24:00.220
But I won't let it go how you want!

00:24:00.220 --> 00:24:02.970
I'll overturn this society!

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:04.340
Shinji...

00:24:05.180 --> 00:24:07.460
What are you planning to do?

00:24:08.860 --> 00:24:13.290
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Battlewasp — Summoning Swarm.

00:24:13.570 --> 00:24:15.560
The fun is only getting started!
